{
  "description": "The Instance v1 document marks almost no response member required, and the legacy Instance API it describes sends null, not \"\", for a string with no value, so convert leaves this document's plain strings optional (NULL_STRINGS in scripts/convert.ts). These members were set on every response in two probes of the live Project on 2026-10-14 (zones fr-par-1/2/3, nl-ams-1/2/3, pl-waw-1/2/3 and it-mil-1: server, volume and image catalogues, the dashboard and every list; in nl-ams-1 a STARDUST1-S server with a routed IPv4 and a routed IPv6 address, two security groups with three rules, a placement group, a private NIC, a local volume, a snapshot and an image, each created, read, updated and listed; 19,677 observations of these members, none null or absent; the second probe decoded every response under ResponseValidation.strict): the identifiers, names, zones, Projects and Organizations of servers, IPs, security groups and their rules, placement groups, private NICs, snapshots and images, the server's commercial type, hostname, MAC address and state detail, its public IPs and location, server type SKUs and GPU names, task links, volume type names; and the resource every Create/Get/Update response wraps (`GetServerResponse.server`, `CreateIpResponse.ip`, ...). Left optional because they were null: `Ip.address` (routed IPv6), `Ip.prefix` (routed IPv4), `SecurityGroup.description` (none given); and because the probe never saw them set: `ServerIpv6`, `ServerMaintenance`, `ServerFilesystem` and `Volume` members (`Volume` is also the SetImage request's `extra_volumes` value, so requiring its members would make callers send them).",
  "patches": [
